 - Outputs/reference files should be JSON arrays. Each element may be a string or object containing `text`/`output` fields.
 - Future work: support tabular CSV, scored datasets, multi-turn conversations.
 
+## Thresholds
+- `generateReport` accepts an optional `thresholds` object (e.g., `{ exact_match: 0.9 }`) to gate on metric scores.
+- Thresholds fail when a metric's score is below the minimum or when the metric has no score (null).
+- JSON reports include `passed` (boolean) and `thresholds` (array) fields when thresholds are specified; Markdown reports include a "Thresholds" section.
+- CLI `--threshold` option parses `metric=min` format, validates that min is 0–1, and exits with code 1 on threshold failure, code 2 on usage error, or code 0 if all pass.
+
 ## Extensibility Hooks
 - `frai-core/src/eval/metrics.js` exposes `DEFAULT_METRICS`; additional metrics can be registered by passing custom evaluators to `runEvaluations`.
 - `writeReport` accepts `format` argument to enable additional exporters (HTML, CSV) later.
